       The flat zero was folded 180 deg the wrong way: at hip_abd = 0 the thigh
       hung UNDER its pitch motor, where the built robot has it ON TOP.  Every
       leg body's geoms, sites and inertial are rolled 180 deg about x --
       pos (x,y,z)->(x,-y,-z), quat pre-multiplied by Rx(180 deg), inertia ixy
       and ixz negated -- and the `stand` keyframe's twelve joint entries are
       negated.  Body `pos`, the absent body `quat`s and all twelve joint
       `axis` attributes are untouched, which is what keeps the body frames
       trunk-aligned at zero and the joint axes right-handed (+x, +z, +z).

       `build_dog6_mjcf.py` in D:\mujoco\dog6_description does NOT do this
       yet.  Rebuilding without applying the same roll silently reverts the
       robot's calibrated zero.  See sim/coordinates.py, "THE ZERO". -->
